==Dutch==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|nl|dum|nichte}}, from {{inh|nl|odt|*nift}}, from {{inh|nl|gmw-pro|*nifti}}, from {{inh|nl|gem-pro|*niftiz}}, from {{inh|nl|ine-pro|*néptih₂}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|nl|/nɪxt/}}
* {{audio|nl|Nl-nicht.ogg}}
* {{hyphenation|nl|nicht}}
* {{rhymes|nl|ɪxt|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{nl-noun|f|-en|nichtje}}

# {{topics|nl|Family members}} [[female]] [[cousin]]; daughter of someone's uncle or aunt
#: {{ux|nl|Mijn '''nicht''' is een jaar jonger dan ik en we zijn goede vriendinnen.|My '''female cousin''' is one year younger than me, and we are good friends.}}
# {{topics|nl|Family members}}[[niece]]; daughter of someone's brother or sister
#: {{ux|nl|Mijn broer en zijn vrouw hebben twee '''nichten''', een tweeling.|My brother and his wife have two '''nieces''', twins.}}
# {{topics|nl|Family members}} [[niece]]; daughter of someone's brother- or sister-in-law
#: {{ux|nl|Mijn oom van vaders kant heeft drie '''nichten''', waarvan er twee getrouwd zijn.|My paternal uncle has three '''nieces''', two of whom are married.}}

====Alternative forms====
