==German==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|de|nich|nich'||informal writing, reflecting the common pronunciation}}
* {{alter|de|net|nit||colloquial; in central Germany, southern Germany, Austria}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|niwiht}}, {{m|gmh|niweht}}, {{m|gmh|niht}}, a contracted form of {{inh|de|goh|niowiht}}, from {{m|goh|nio||never}} + {{m|goh|wiht||being, creature}}, the last from {{der|de|gem-pro|*wihtą}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/nɪçt/}}
** {{IPA|de|[nɪçt]|aa=predominant}}
** {{IPA|de|[niçt]|aa=Bavaria; parts of Austria; Ruhrgebiet}}
** {{IPA|de|[nɪxt]|[nixt]|[-χt]|aa=Switzerland; parts of Austria}}
** {{IPA|de|[nɪɕt]|[nəɕt]|[-ʃt]|aa=parts of central Germany}}
* {{IPA|de|/nɪç/|aa=common speech; quasi-standard in northern and central Germany; alternations as above}}
* {{audio|de|De-nicht.ogg}}
* {{audio|de|De-nicht2.ogg}}
* {{rhymes|de|ɪçt|ɪç|s1=1}}

===Adverb===
{{de-adv}}

# [[not]], [[non-]] {{gloss|''negates the meaning of a verb, adjective, or adverb''}}
#: {{ux|de|Bitte '''nicht''' stören!|Please do '''not''' disturb!}}
#: {{ux|de|Das ist '''nicht''' wahr.|That is '''not''' true.}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|de|nichtig}}
** {{l|de|Nichtigkeit}}

===Interjection===
{{head|de|interjection|head=nicht?}}

# {{lb|de|tag question|dated|or|formal}} [[right]]?; is it?; is it not?
#: {{syn|de|gell|ne|nicht wahr|oder|[[oder]] [[nicht]]|wa}}
#: {{ux|de|Du bist sicher die Claudia, '''nicht?'''|You must be Claudia, '''aren't you?'''}}

